Bb4 6. Nxc6 bxc6 { Taking towards the centre. Our pawns are doubled but we will push ...d5 next. } 7. Bd3 d5 8. exd5 { By far the most popular. } O-O { Black usually plays 8...cxd5 which is not bad but we have another idea in mind. } 9. O-O { -KEY- } Bg4 $5 ( { A fresh idea, which occured in high-level practice in 2018. It allows Black to equalize in a dynamic way, without need of delving into the intricacies of various move orders after the automatic } 9... cxd5 ) 
